# Exam track — Theme: Tourismus am Heemechtsland — Sub-lesson 2: Key Phrases
# Plain sentences (no @question): presented in either direction.
#
# These phrases are grounded in the user's real interview answers (2026-09-01,
# home country: Ukraine) — do not "improve" or genericize them in a later
# editing pass. Shorter restatements of the same facts drilled in depth in
# 03_questions.letz.

@lesson T1.02 "Tourism Phrases"

@word schéin = beautiful
@word frëndlech = friendly
@word historesch = historical
@word interessant = interesting
@word geféierlech = dangerous
@word deier = expensive
@word gënschteg = affordable
@word frësch = fresh
@word staark = strong
@word berouegend = calming
@word aktiv = active
@word entspaant = relaxed
@word besonnesch = special
@word wëllkomm = welcome
@word gesond = healthy
@word extrem = extreme
@word modern = modern
@word sonneg = sunny
@word waarm = warm
@word kal = cold
@word de Wanter = the winter
@word de Summer = the summer
@word d'Mëschung = the mixture
@word d'Wolleken = the clouds
@word d'Sonn = the sun
@word sech entspanen = to relax
@word hëllefen = to help

@sentence
@lu D'Natur an der Ukrain ass schéin a berouegend.
@en The nature in Ukraine is beautiful and calming.
@distractor-lu Stied
@distractor-lu deier
@distractor-en cities
@distractor-en expensive

@sentence
@lu Mir hunn eng gesond Mëschung vu Sonn a Wolleken.
@en We have a healthy mixture of sun and clouds.
@distractor-lu Gepäck
@distractor-lu Muséeën
@distractor-en luggage
@distractor-en museums

@sentence
@lu D'Leit am Weste si besonnesch frëndlech.
@en The people in the west are especially friendly.
@distractor-lu geféierlech
@distractor-lu ni
@distractor-en dangerous
@distractor-en never

@sentence
@lu De Kaffi zu Kiew an zu Lwiw ass eng besonnesch Erfarung.
@en The coffee in Kyiv and Lviv is a special experience.
@distractor-lu Zuch
@distractor-lu schlecht
@distractor-en train
@distractor-en bad

@sentence
@lu D'ukrainesch Kichen ass bekannt a ganz gutt.
@en The Ukrainian cuisine is well-known and very good.
@distractor-lu onbekannt
@distractor-lu kal
@distractor-en unknown
@distractor-en cold

@sentence
@lu Ech fuere gär mam Nuetszuch duerch d'Land.
@en I like taking the night train through the country.
@distractor-lu Kaffi
@distractor-lu ni
@distractor-en coffee
@distractor-en never

@sentence
@lu Am Summer wandere mir gär an de Karpaten.
@en In summer we like hiking in the Carpathians.
@distractor-lu Wanter
@distractor-lu schwammen
@distractor-en winter
@distractor-en swim

@sentence
@lu D'Stëmmung op de Festivaller ass ëmmer flott.
@en The atmosphere at the festivals is always nice.
@distractor-lu deier
@distractor-lu kal
@distractor-en expensive
@distractor-en cold

@sentence
@lu Vill Touriste wëllen Tschernobyl gesinn.
@en Many tourists want to see Chernobyl.
@distractor-lu Gepäck
@distractor-lu kafen
@distractor-en luggage
@distractor-en buy

@sentence
@lu Ech hunn d'Ukrain als Tourist entdeckt.
@en I discovered Ukraine as a tourist.
@distractor-lu verkaaft
@distractor-lu Wieder
@distractor-en sold
@distractor-en weather

@sentence
@lu Wann Dir d'Ukrain besichtegt, sidd Dir wëllkomm.
@en If you visit Ukraine, you are welcome.
@distractor-lu Gepäck
@distractor-lu ni
@distractor-en luggage
@distractor-en never
